{"author":"Robert Jamieson, A. R. Fausset and David Brown","book":"Commentary Critical and Explanatory on the Whole Bible","chapter":614,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:jfb:Ps.136","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"Robert Jamieson, A. R. Fausset and David Brown","authorshipDateRange":"19th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Protestant","translator":null,"edition":"1871 one-volume text; expanded electronic edition by Ernie Stefanik","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"jfb","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/jamieson/jfb.html","title":"Commentary Critical and Explanatory on the Whole Bible"},"searchIndexed":false},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"jfb","source":{"id":"jfb","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/jamieson/jfb.html","title":"Commentary Critical and Explanatory on the Whole Bible"},"title":"Psalms 136","reference":"Psalms 136","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"PSALM 136","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"Ps 136:1-26.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":3,"text":"The theme is the same as that of Psalm 135.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":4,"text":"God should be praised for His works of creation and providence, His deliverance and care of His people, and judgments on their enemies, and His goodness to all.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":5,"text":"The chorus to every verse is in terms of that of Ps 106:1; 118:1-4, and was perhaps used as the Amen by the people, in worship (compare 1Ch 16:36; Ps 105:45).","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":6,"text":"1-3.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":7,"text":"The divine titles denote supremacy.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":8,"text":"4. alone—excluding all help.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":9,"text":"5, 6. by wisdom—or, \"in wisdom\" (Ps 104:24).","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":10,"text":"made—literally, \"maker of.\"","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":11,"text":"above the waters—or, \"higher than the waters\" (Ps 24:2).","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":12,"text":"12.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":13,"text":"Compare similar expressions (Ex 3:20; De 4:34, &c.).","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":14,"text":"15. overthrew—literally, \"shook off,\" as in Ex 14:27, as a contemptuous rejection of a reptile.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":15,"text":"23. remembered us—or, \"for us\" (Ps 132:1).","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":23,"scriptureVerseEnd":23},{"verse":16,"text":"our low estate—that is, captivity.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":23,"scriptureVerseEnd":23},{"verse":17,"text":"24.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":24,"scriptureVerseEnd":24},{"verse":18,"text":"And hath redeemed us—or, literally, \"snatched us\"—alluding to the sudden deliverance effected by the overthrow of Babylon.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":24,"scriptureVerseEnd":24},{"verse":19,"text":"25.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":25,"scriptureVerseEnd":25},{"verse":20,"text":"To the special favors to His people is added the record of God's goodness to all His creatures (compare Mt 6:30).","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":25,"scriptureVerseEnd":25},{"verse":21,"text":"26.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26},{"verse":22,"text":"God of heaven—occurs but once (Jon 1:9) before the captivity.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26},{"verse":23,"text":"It is used by the later writers as specially distinguishing God from idols.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":136}}